ne","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T20:52:25-07:00","id":1520741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520738#post1520738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way we'll get V6 is if it's sold off and that largely depends on whether or not Bloodlines 2 flops.</div> </div> </div> </div>With how long it has been in development for, all the controversies surrounding it, and the current trend of video game companies, I wouldn't be surprised if it does flop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T20:56:53-07:00","id":1520742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520741#post1520741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With how long it has been in development for, all the controversies surrounding it, and the current trend of video game companies, I wouldn't be surprised if it does flop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh. I hope it does flop. V5 was terrible and I hate what Paradox has been doing with the IP<br /> <br /> The only good thing to come from the Paradox buyout was the Storytellers Vault","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T22:03:55-07:00","id":1520744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520742#post1520742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh. I hope it does flop. V5 was terrible and I hate what Paradox has been doing with the IP<br /> <br /> The only good thing to come from the Paradox buyout was the Storytellers Vault</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I agree, if the franchise as a whole doesn't seem profitable it's more likely that they'll just stop the investment and the franchise will stay put for a few years, that's if they don't want to sell to someone interested, but that could even be worse .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T22:07:52-07:00","id":1520746,"title":"","content":"I think they maybe rebbot to please a new audience or deliver WOD as a shared universe with another franchise, of course, with the necessary changes. Otherwise, they'll wait a few years to do something new with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T02:45:02-07:00","id":1520753,"title":"","content":"I would hope that they don't go back and forth between developing games, giving up on on them and repackaging Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T06:57:29-07:00","id":1520766,"title":"","content":"I sincerely hope that V5 dies, and that all this woke crap dies with it.<br /> I hope the new creative and design team has the balls to look at the V5 crap and say, &quot;ok let's go in the opposite direction from that, let's evaluate what are the best mechanics of Requiem 2ed and let's incorporate that into a Vampire 6ed and reestablish the cannon.<br /> Is it so difficult to see the efficiency of the rules and mechanics of Requiem 2ed and adapt it for the V6?<br /> And one last thing, please decide, either Blood Potency or Generation, the two together is not efficient, and just confusing; how I wish Hunger Dice and Mess Critical were eliminated, along with all those vanilla clan concepts\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T09:24:32-07:00","id":1520769,"title":"","content":"If there is going to be a V6 tabletop edition, I would hope that the game line just goes full modular rather than trying to be a meta-narrative game space. Or in less fancy terms, just provide the framework for the World of Darkness and let people pick and choose their own politics and factions that reside in that space.<br /> <br /> Part of what messed up the reception of V5 was both the very clunky reshuffle the status quo and then the more modern political messaging being shoehorned into the base game.<br /> <br /> The game line should give mechanical frameworks for running the system with the original Camarilla vs. Sabbat vs. Anarchs setup, there should be a framework for only having one faction be the only one, there should be a version where all the clans all exist in one underground city and each &quot;faction&quot; is a essentially a political party, etc. basically however you want to experiment with the setting is supported. So rather than saying your head canon is X, you just say I am using setting X, with Clans Y, and Politics Z in my current game.<br /> <br /> I would hope someone does an XP rebalance, so each character build is more functional for the time spent. Half the builds I tend to want to play will never be finished let alone expanded on by the time the others have hit full functionality, or the game has ended.<br /> <br /> But if I am being completely honest, if there is going to be a new version of Vampire, my bet would be on a digital product rather than a physical one. Think of each splat line having its own custom digital tabletop RP app. It would be little more than a video chat room or virtual idol chat with ST tools and a digital database for the rules. The character sheets, notes, dice rolling, etc are all digital and have multimedia integration.<br /> <br /> As for Bloodlines 2.... it is stuck between a rock and hard place. As a current year game it will never be true enough to the source material to please older fans, while at the same time it has to avoid that source material to have a chance at appealing to younger generations.<br /> <br /> What I wouldn't give for 11 Bit studios (This War of Mine / Frostpunk) to do something with the VtM setting. They seem to have a better understanding of humanity issues than most developers, less good vs. bad and more figuring out a way to live with yourself when you did what was needed to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T11:15:53-07:00","id":1520778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520769#post1520769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game line should give mechanical frameworks for running the system with the original Camarilla vs. Sabbat vs. Anarchs setup, there should be a framework for only having one faction be the only one, there should be a version where all the clans all exist in one underground city and each &quot;faction&quot; is a essentially a political party, etc. basically however you want to experiment with the setting is supported. So rather than saying your head canon is X, you just say I am using setting X, with Clans Y, and Politics Z in my current game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds similar to Covenants from VTR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520769#post1520769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But if I am being completely honest, if there is going to be a new version of Vampire, my bet would be on a digital product rather than a physical one. Think of each splat line having its own custom digital tabletop RP app. It would be little more than a video chat room or virtual idol chat with ST tools and a digital database for the rules. The character sheets, notes, dice rolling, etc are all digital and have multimedia integration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am legit surprised that they havent tried to do this yet, it feels like the best thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T11:55:08-07:00","id":1520781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520778#post1520778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds similar to Covenants from VTR.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of &quot;All Flesh Must Be Eaten&quot; where the modules allow for whole different genres and rule sets. Yes that would dilute the VtM brand a bit, but that specific flavor seems to be generation-centric and an acquired taste to others.<br /> <br /> Admittedly this is in part due to my own proclivity for doing spin off &quot;what if&quot; games. As an example, I ran one game where the Giovanni plan happened, but it changed the setting in a way no one expected. Rather than bringing down the veil, it just caused all dead humans to reanimate as Romero type zombies. The vampire PCs are now faced with the fact that the masquerade doesn't matter anymore, but more importantly, how do vampires keep humans alive to be their food source? You have your basic vampire issues, but also societal engineering and city state formation &amp; governance.<br /> <br /> Perhaps one of the more common debates about vampire populations could also be addressed in the same fashion that fantasy games suggest doing no magic worlds, low magic worlds, or high magic worlds. Imagine how the setting would change if vampires couldn't automatically embrace, it was something they had to acquire like leveling up a discipline or had to roll a check to survive the attempt at creating a childer. The vampiric population of the world would tiny by comparison, which in turn would change the factions, the politics, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T12:10:42-07:00","id":1520783,"title":"","content":"Just make Chronicles of Darkness and World of Darkness open source at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T12:29:45-07:00","id":1520784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520783#post1520783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make Chronicles of Darkness and World of Darkness open source at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> The Storytellers Vault is the one good thing that came from the Paradox buyout and I hope it can help set some sort of precedent for an open source take on all the previous versions of WoD and CofD/nWoD. I know STV is not the same as an open source deal but hopefully it could be a step in the right direction.<br /> <br /> If they made WoD open source, I'd do a shot-for-shot remake of VTM 1E and then move on from there, wiping away all the metaplot and starting anew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T13:06:29-07:00","id":1520785,"title":"","content":"I like V5, but I wish they would do some more setting and lore stuff for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T13:17:56-07:00","id":1520786,"title":"","content":"Going &quot;open source&quot; would be a giant dick-punch to Onyx Path considering that would destroy their ability to make money off of Exalted in the process.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't give Paradox too much credit for the STV. I'd bet a considerable amount of money on that happening regardless (mostly because OBS, the company that runs DTRPG and all those community content services like STV, is owned by one of the original WW founders and even during the CCP days that lead to a close relationship between the people making the games and getting into those outlets).<br /> <br /> While I would like Paradox to sell off the IPs, I don't think that's happening any time soon. They're acting like they can turn a profit here, and they're going to want to at least break even on their initial investment rather than take a large loss to off-load the property. Nobody is paying them the price they paid for it given its current state; unless some fan wins the lottery and doesn't give a shit about making money and just wants to pick who makes the books instead.<br /> <br /> I think the most likely thing for the WoD is what WotC wants to do with D&amp;D: hop on the live service model. Sure, still do physical copies and all, but those are already going up a lot in price because they're luxury items. A cloud library of books that can be edited whenever Paradox wants, that we never own any part of and just rent access to, is exactly the kind of thing business think is a good idea no matter how much customers actually hate it and only use them because we're not given a fair choice. No more editions, just patches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T08:08:31-07:00","id":1520819,"title":"","content":"Provide the rules as open source, and then provide campaign books that move the metaplot. People who play masquerade want the setting and the metaplot, otherwise they'd just play Requiem which has better rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T10:38:05-07:00","id":1520823,"title":"","content":"Even as someone that prefers that CofD rules over any iteration of the WoD rules so far, I know people that stick to the older rules specifically because for some people things like familiarity are &quot;better.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, you can't keep the core rules to just one game line. The entire WoD, Scion 1e, Trinity 1e, and Exalted all technically run on the same rules you're talking about making open source. You can't just make that system open source for VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T12:42:45-07:00","id":1520831,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna say something super dramatic/controversial (though correct):<br /> <br /> V5 is bloody great<br /> The &quot;woke shit&quot; is here to stay, like it or not.<br /> Vampire brings in plenty of money and is growing as a brand.<br /> They got rid of the meta plot because WE bitched and bitched claiming we hate it.<br /> WE said the only good thing about CoD was the ruleset, so they used a bunch of it.<br /> WE made the Sabbat one dimensional powergamey murderhobos so they had to take it away, that way the entire line doesn't get painted by those that prefer that style of gameplay.<br /> <br /> Thats not to say, Onyx Path and Paradox haven't stumbled here and there, but all in all they modernized a product that we have been circle jerking over for the last 20 years and brought us into the 2020s and <b><i>marketing to new fans with modern sensibilities</i></b>.<br /> We need to accept that what was acceptable in 1990 is not acceptable in 2020 (shocker, I know).<br /> The times has evolved, and the brand evolved with it. They aren't marketing to us old timers. We have less time, and less disposable income. <br /> <br /> V6 (if it happens) will continue this trend. The social landscape has been evolving quickly even, since the launch of V5, to the point that in the time it takes to write, edit, print, and distribute a book, things have changed. This is affecting all areas of entertainment, from movies to TV to music, video games etc etc. The Vault is incredible and allows us as a community to get work out there, faster than Paradox can market to the world. <br /> <br /> I think V6 will happen in 5-10 years and will likely be more directed towards online use, since it seems that the majority of games take place online.<br /> <br /> Cheers, and back into my hole where I'll continue to play with a bunch of old people and a couple of babies ;P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T14:13:00-07:00","id":1520833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520831#post1520831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need to accept that what was acceptable in 1990 is not acceptable in 2020 (shocker, I know).</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two can play this game: THEY need to accept the fact that in the 2020s, as opposed to the 1990s, WE receive more information about their products before they hit the shelves (digital or otherwise) and, based upon this info, we can choose to simply not purchase said products, therefore depriving them of cash, ruining their profit projections and turning certain hits into unexpected flops. Will it kill WoD5? Uncertain, but possible. Will it prevent WoD5 contending with D&amp;D for the title of &quot;Number One RPG&quot; like in the 1990s due to the fanbase being overly fractured? Most definitely.</span><br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>One thing is for sure: nothing is for sure.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/83-evolved_lupus","name":"evolved_lupus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar83_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T15:02:47-07:00","id":1520834,"title":"","content":"This might be pointlessly yelling into the void (and very repetitive for things I've been saying here for years...):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520831#post1520831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;woke shit&quot; is here to stay, like it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great if true. The problem is that Paradox has demonstrated they're not woke, they're performative. They're not dedicated to progressive causes as a company, but want enough credit with their left-leaning customer base that they'll act &quot;woke&quot; enough to look good to people that aren't in the loop with their less then great business decisions from this perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire brings in plenty of money and is growing as a brand. </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.<br /> <br /> Also, where's my Bloodlines 2?<br /> <br /> Consider that in the 5 years since V5 core released, it's averaged about four source books a year (including things like the quickstart, and books that have reprinted material so you can get the rules for all the Clans without being forced to buy books you might not otherwise want), between nWW/Paradox and <b>five</b> publishing partners. That's six different studios, over five years, averaging four TTRPG products a year...that's a lot of resources for not a lot of &quot;growth.&quot; Because there's a big difference between gross and net. Also the brand has... gotten a reputation for decent but nothing special Interactive Fiction? There's no indication that the traditional fiction or comics are being pursued as something to promote the brand more, Swansong and Bloodhunt hurt the brand as a video game seller (kinda sad for a video game company), and still no TV/movie/etc. in sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They got rid of the meta plot because WE bitched and bitched claiming we hate it.<br /> WE said the only good thing about CoD was the ruleset, so they used a bunch of it.<br /> WE made the Sabbat one dimensional powergamey murderhobos so they had to take it away, that way the entire line doesn't get painted by those that prefer that style of gameplay. </div> </div> </div>Who's this &quot;We&quot; you keep talking for?<br /> <br /> The original WW, not Paradox's short lived WW revival, ended the metaplot in 2003, and when they started the 20th books (even if they only did one of them) under CCP, they chose to keep those metaplot agnostic. Paradox brought the metaplot back. Not only did the story move forward 20 years, the story has shifted as supplements have come out.<br /> <br /> Lots of people here and elsewhere have been singing much higher praises of the CofD than just its rules.<br /> <br /> People that want to play one dimensional power-gaming murderhobos could do it in VtM just fine without the Sabbat... they still can since the Anarchs in V5 are fine with that apparently. The idea that they &quot;had&quot; to take it away for some PR reasons is bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thats not to say, Onyx Path and Paradox haven't stumbled here and there, but all in all they modernized a product that we have been circle jerking over for the last 20 years and brought us into the 2020s and <b><i>marketing to new fans with modern sensibilities</i></b>. </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path didn't make V5 what it is, they did a few sources books for it under Paradox's direction.<br /> <br /> Also... the idea that V5 is particularly modern, or particularly well suited to marketing to a new generation is kinda laughable. The whole marketing scheme so far is, &quot;Hey we were big in the late 90s, and we have a new book with rules that would be considered innovative in 2005, also we changed the setting in ways that mean nothing to you because you're new and have no idea what that means to the last four editions!&quot;<br /> <br /> [quote]We need to accept that what was acceptable in 1990 is not acceptable in 2020 (shocker, I know).<br /> <br /> Who hasn't accepted that? There's a huge difference between not agreeing that the WoD needed a major overhaul, and not agreeing that V5 did a good job of it. Look over in the WtA forums. The Ghost Council that we could have gotten is pretty popular compared to the one we got. People want change, but not change for the sake of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The times has evolved, and the brand evolved with it. They aren't marketing to us old timers. We have less time, and less disposable income. </div> </div> </div>V5 references far too much old stuff to say it's not marketed towards us. They kept the names Reckoning and Apocalypse despite being extremely different core premises to their original counterparts with those titles for H5 and W5, and only us old timers are attached to those names. We might have less time, but we actually have more money... jobs and shit is why we don't have time like we used to, but most of us oldies have also be working long enough to not be stuck at barely afford rent/mortgage stage at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V6 (if it happens) will continue this trend. The social landscape has been evolving quickly even,.. </div> </div> </div>Here's a great example of something smart CofD does: it's not pegged to social commentary that's only relevant to one era. That strategy might make it less hard hitting as the WoD can be, but it also means CofD material isn't socially out of date before it's published.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think V6 will happen in 5-10 years and will likely be more directed towards online use, since it seems that the majority of games take place online. </div> </div> </div>More online focus is definitely the future... not sure why you'd think that's controversial when putting out digital material for VTTs is fairy common these days (and something WoD5 already does).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T15:26:47-07:00","id":1520839,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know what will happen and I hope that the line isn't discontinued again as I've been enjoying having an old friend back in the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T19:44:42-07:00","id":1520852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520833#post1520833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two can play this game: THEY need to accept the fact that in the 2020s, as opposed to the 1990s, WE receive more information about their products before they hit the shelves (digital or otherwise) and, based upon this info, we can choose to simply not purchase said products, therefore depriving them of cash, ruining their profit projections and turning certain hits into unexpected flops. Will it kill WoD5? Uncertain, but possible. Will it prevent WoD5 contending with D&amp;D for the title of &quot;Number One RPG&quot; like in the 1990s due to the fanbase being overly fractured? Most definitely.</span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, too much of a luddite to quote properly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot; That would be great if true. The problem is that Paradox has demonstrated they're not woke, they're performative. They're not dedicated to progressive causes as a company, but want enough credit with their left-leaning customer base that they'll act &quot;woke&quot; enough to look good to people that aren't in the loop with their less then great business decisions from this perspective.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think they are trying. are they pandering? 100%. But I think the authors are trying, and I don't envy them. It must be hard to try to write for a varied audience while not pissing off a vocal few<br /> <br /> &quot;Citation needed.<br /> <br /> Also, where's my Bloodlines 2?<br /> <br /> Consider that in the 5 years since V5 core released, it's averaged about four source books a year (including things like the quickstart, and books that have reprinted material so you can get the rules for all the Clans without being forced to buy books you might not otherwise want), between nWW/Paradox and <b>five</b> publishing partners. That's six different studios, over five years, averaging four TTRPG products a year...that's a lot of resources for not a lot of &quot;growth.&quot; Because there's a big difference between gross and net. Also the brand has... gotten a reputation for decent but nothing special Interactive Fiction? There's no indication that the traditional fiction or comics are being pursued as something to promote the brand more, Swansong and Bloodhunt hurt the brand as a video game seller (kinda sad for a video game company), and still no TV/movie/etc. in sight.\u200b&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Don't really need one, since in most places I look, the original books are sold out and ppl are begging for reprints. I agree, the slow launch of books is concerning though with the price of the books, my wallet is happier. As for the 5 studios, as I recall, and correct me if I'm wrong, but it seems that with every studio, there was drama over something that was written. To me it looks like 'ok these guys fucked up, more bad press, on to the next'<br /> <br /> Bloodlines 2 is a game and a totally different department, but looks like a clusterfuck, and after the Cyberpunk debacle, I'm sure they're treading carefully. Speaking of, weren't we supposed to get an update this month? Or did I miss it?<br /> <br /> As for other media, there was rumor of a movie or a show, not sure what happened to that, but the strike certainly isn't speeding up that process. Everyone touts Paradox as a massive video game development company (which they are) but keep in mind the games they specialize in. Bloodlines better not be anything like Crusader Kings or Europa. Bloodhunt seemed like a catering to the folks that like shooters, and introducing them to the brand. I thought Swansong was great, same with the visual novels. Great stories and a great look at what the game could be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;Who's this &quot;We&quot; you keep talking for?<br /> <br /> The original WW, not Paradox's short lived WW revival, ended the metaplot in 2003, and when they started the 20th books (even if they only did one of them) under CCP, they chose to keep those metaplot agnostic. Paradox brought the metaplot back. Not only did the story move forward 20 years, the story has shifted as supplements have come out.<br /> <br /> Lots of people here and elsewhere have been singing much higher praises of the CofD than just its rules.<br /> <br /> People that want to play one dimensional power-gaming murderhobos could do it in VtM just fine without the Sabbat... they still can since the Anarchs in V5 are fine with that apparently. The idea that they &quot;had&quot; to take it away for some PR reasons is bullshit.\u200b&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The WE is US. The vocal fanbase. I'm not speaking for anyone, just pointing out the hypocrisy I see, thus why I stopped going on forums and such. On this very forum for years I watched people complain about the metaplot. Like when BJD was released tons of people complained &quot;I hate the metaplot&quot;&quot;CoD sucks except for the rules&quot; and in this very thread &quot; I hope they knock it off with all the woke shit&quot; So the authors changed shit. And here now I see &quot;I hate they took out the metaplot&quot;&quot;Its just CoD rules in VTM&quot; etc<br /> <br /> I've been around since V1 and I watched all this unfold in real time as I'm sure many others have. Paradox brought it back because it was good and kept folks buying books. But this time they painted a very broad picture like CoD did, instead of narrowing it down with huge events every year. And that still draws complaints. It like a no win scenario.<br /> <br /> All I saw from the release of CoD was complaints (and to be fair, I was among them though less vocal)<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<i>&quot;Onyx Path didn't make V5 what it is, they did a few sources books for it under Paradox's direction.<br /> <br /> Also... the idea that V5 is particularly modern, or particularly well suited to marketing to a new generation is kinda laughable. The whole marketing scheme so far is, &quot;Hey we were big in the late 90s, and we have a new book with rules that would be considered innovative in 2005, also we changed the setting in ways that mean nothing to you because you're new and have no idea what that means to the last four editions!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We need to accept that what was acceptable in 1990 is not acceptable in 2020 (shocker, I know).<br /> <br /> Who hasn't accepted that? There's a huge difference between not agreeing that the WoD needed a major overhaul, and not agreeing that V5 did a good job of it. Look over in the WtA forums. The Ghost Council that we could have gotten is pretty popular compared to the one we got. People want change, but not change for the sake of it.\u200b&quot; </div> </div> </div></i><br /> <br /> <br /> Including the first book BJD - which created a buzz, and to this day I see people in various forums looking for the books that have x event they'd like further explanation of. Its neat to me, watching old timers lay out the events that lead to now to the young ones, and seeing the enthusiasm. Its like music - what do you mean x band had 5 more albums before the big hit of today?!<br /> On a side note I saw Pantera the other day, and seeing the kids who were like &quot;my older brother loved this band and now I finally get to see them. Now its my turn&quot; I feel like much the same thing is happening with VTM. Its not our game anymore. Its moved on and now a bunch of kids have taken over and sometimes I find myself annoyed, but more often I smile like a grandfather who has given his grandkid his old car. lol fuck I'm old.<br /> <br /> to the second quote &quot;<i>Who hasn't accepted that? There's a huge difference between not agreeing that the WoD needed a major overhaul, and not agreeing that V5 did a good job of it.</i>\u200b&quot;<br /> In this very thread we see people who haven't accepted it. V5 did a great job. Full stop. And it was needed. Does each of us have different ideas for or tables? Yes, of course. Its like everyone wanted them to produce the game perfect for their table, which is impossible. As for WTA all I see is &quot;they took away our Get, stupid woke culture&quot; and I stop reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>V5 references far too much old stuff to say it's not marketed towards us. They kept the names Reckoning and Apocalypse despite being extremely different core premises to their original counterparts with those titles for H5 and W5, and only us old timers are attached to those names. We might have less time, but we actually have more money... jobs and shit is why we don't have time like we used to, but most of us oldies have also be working long enough to not be stuck at barely afford rent/mortgage stage at this point.</i> </div> </div> </div>They mention the old stuff for a couple reasons, as a nod to us to keep us engaged, and to keep the kids buying. Also some of the old fans are now authors themselves, so of course they are going to include the shit they love. The second part is debatable. I work in entertainment and we time shit for major holidays/vacation times, and when student loans are released. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Here's a great example of something smart CofD does: it's not pegged to social commentary that's only relevant to one era. That strategy might make it less hard hitting as the WoD can be, but it also means CofD material isn't socially out of date before it's published.</i> </div> </div> </div>I agree and I'd also argue that I think WoD is kind of pushed into it socially, for better or worse<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>More online focus is definitely the future... not sure why you'd think that's controversial when putting out digital material for VTTs is fairy common these days (and something WoD5 already does)</i> </div> </div> </div>They kinda do but they are slow as hell with that too<br /> <br /> Anyways, great discussion dude, glad we can have it without yelling and screaming and cursing at each other","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T02:04:58-07:00","id":1520860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520852#post1520852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they are trying. are they pandering? 100%. But I think the authors are trying, and I don't envy them. It must be hard to try to write for a varied audience while not pissing off a vocal few\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had multiple creatives and community volunteers come forward (since before V5 was even in alpha test state) pointing out that no, it's just pandering and no they're not trying to do more than pander and manage PR. Some of the authors most certain have tried, but they're the one's Paradox have driven off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't really need one, since in most places I look, the original books are sold out and ppl are begging for reprints. </div> </div> </div>You kinda do, because anecdote isn't data. One of the stores around here has a first printing V5 core hard copy at 25% off and nobody's bothered buying it, let alone asked for more stock to get ordered.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's a simple explanation beyond how much living in a small town rural area means local group preferences which are by no means indicative of the whole audience in the world skews things: too many of us order our stuff online because our public transit sucks and none of the stores that sell TTRPG books can afford big enough spaces towards things like having play areas in the store to build a community around. Why try to find ~1 hr of time to get to a store, maybe more to try out the second, and plenty of gas money to go along with it, when it can just arrive on my doorstep and the shipping doesn't feel so bad compared to when gas was cheaper and I had way more free time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the 5 studios, as I recall, and correct me if I'm wrong, but it seems that with every studio, there was drama over something that was written. To me it looks like 'ok these guys fucked up, more bad press, on to the next' </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the bad press has pretty much been on Paradox's shoulders for demands they're making of studios (plus plenty of dumb things they've said in response t various PR issues). Modiphus was dropped as what seems to be more of a business incompatibility with distribution than content (since Paradox was still doing most of the content then, and was heavily involved in the few books Modiphius did. The only controversies with Onyx Path were things like the entire W20 team at Onyx Path giving up on new books until Apocalyptic Record because they were tired of Paradox forcing them to put in bad content. None of the Hunter's Entertainment books were particularly controversial, but we've heard a lot about how much tension there was because that team wanted H5 and W5 to be more like V5 (be an update and continuation of the older game instead of a full reboot). Though Sambrano's treatment while a member of the Hunter's W5 team is another PR blunder complete on Paradox's shoulders. Epic - like Onyx Path for that matter - hasn't been &quot;dropped&quot; as much as not offered any new jobs because Epic's only contributions to the TTRPG books is based on their video game. And Renegade is the current primary WoD5 partner studio.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bloodlines 2 is a game and a totally different department, but looks like a clusterfuck, and after the Cyberpunk debacle, I'm sure they're treading carefully. Speaking of, weren't we supposed to get an update this month? Or did I miss it?<br /> <br /> As for other media, there was rumor of a movie or a show, not sure what happened to that, but the strike certainly isn't speeding up that process. Everyone touts Paradox as a massive video game development company (which they are) but keep in mind the games they specialize in. Bloodlines better not be anything like Crusader Kings or Europa. Bloodhunt seemed like a catering to the folks that like shooters, and introducing them to the brand. I thought Swansong was great, same with the visual novels. Great stories and a great look at what the game could be. </div> </div> </div>All of this though, is about the health of the brand as a whole. Paradox didn't buy the WoD to just build up a TTRPG brand from the small audience it held onto under Onyx Path's care, they want an expanded media brand. That's their stated goal in all this. So that media needs to actually be putting a dent in those markets; which is really hard when there isn't even anything new to put out for a lot of them. These things are how Paradox really things the brand will grow. The TTRPGs are like Marvel still making comics even though there are individual MCU movies that made more money than comic books sales have in multiple years: completely abandoning the legacy media form the brand started in would be horrible marketing, but it's not where there's real growth to be had. <br /> <br /> One of the more successful indie devs once broke down the numbers for folks and showed that in practical buying power (that is, not raw dollar amounts) the size of the RPG market has been stagnant since the 2000s recession. Even with all the increased D&amp;D popularity of the last few years, TTRPG books themselves haven't seen any serious increase in how much the general audience is spending relative to things like the costs of production. TTRPG can, basically, only really grow by taking customers from other TTRPGs. Other markets are where there's actual room for growth instead of fighting over how big of a slice of the pie you get is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The WE is US. The vocal fanbase. I'm not speaking for anyone, just pointing out the hypocrisy I see,... </div> </div> </div>You can't have it both ways. Either you are speaking for folks (because you're claiming the entire fanbase is saying specific things), or you're not talkin about the actual vocal fanbase, you're just cherry-picking individual posts.<br /> <br /> A lot of what you're seeing isn't hypocrisy as much as this fanbase not actually being nearly as unified about a lot of things as yous seem to think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It like a no win scenario. </div> </div> </div>Because Paradox doesn't have any idea of what realistically &quot;winning&quot; in the TTRPG space looks like. They're doing... basically what you're doing: taking these really shallow reads of fan reactions, and instead of trying to deep dive into what's really going on, they're just reacting to the surface level stuff. Of course that's a no-win strategy. And if they actually listened more thoroughly, they'd have a much better idea of how to avoid the constant PR problems they keep having.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I saw from the release of CoD was complaints (and to be fair, I was among them though less vocal) </div> </div> </div>That was 19 years ago. The conversation has moved on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Including the first book BJD... </div> </div> </div>BJD wasn't the first V5 book, it was the last V20 book. That's one of the reasons it's actually better at getting older fans and newer fans to talk about lore deep dives than V5 core is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its not our game anymore. Its moved on and now a bunch of kids have taken over and sometimes I find myself annoyed, but more often I smile like a grandfather who has given his grandkid his old car. lol fuck I'm old. </div> </div> </div>While having Outstar be a big public face of the company helps it look younger, the head WoD folks for Paradox have generally been of the older and mid Gen Xers in age range. It's not being run by a whole new generation of folks coming to this with fresh eyes. It's being run by folks that were into it back in the 90s too.<br /> <br /> All three WoD5 core books so far have been worked on by people that worked on TTRPG for the old WW back in the day. The keys didn't get passed on to your grandchildren, they got sold to someone about your age (maybe a few years younger) because that car was cool back in the day to them too, and they're hoping a good paint job can make it cool again to the actual younger generation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this very thread we see people who haven't accepted it. </div> </div> </div>It feels like you're conflating at least to separate things (The need for WoD to adapt to the times, and whether or not V5 did that well).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 did a great job. Full stop. </div> </div> </div>No, it didn't. And to actually make a case instead of assert my feelings as facts: Jason Car (the one that works for Paradox as a brand manager!)l, who runs one of the more popular live-plays for V5, basically doesn't use the books because he ended up using so many house rules and setting homebrew that people actually started complaining that the book they bought didn't seem to be the game he was running.<br /> <br /> If one of the company's top PR folks has to very liberally apply the Golden Rule to make the game functional for live streaming him running it for a group, that's a really big indicator that it did not do a great job.<br /> <br /> It means it has potential, but one I've sen Paradox consistently squander instead of treasure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it was needed. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I'd rather have the VtM edition Rich and Eddy were working on to pitch to CCP before the Paradox buy out. No, it wouldn't have been perfect, it wouldn't appeal to everyone, but I'm fairly confident it would have done all the good things V5 did, but better, and with a much smaller set of major missteps to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for WTA all I see is &quot;they took away our Get, stupid woke culture&quot; and I stop reading. </div> </div> </div>Maybe read past that? Because there's a lot more being discussed than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They mention the old stuff for a couple reasons... </div> </div> </div>Right. It's not just about targeting the new fans and leaving us grognards to either get on board of hoard our old books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second part is debatable. I work in entertainment and we time shit for major holidays/vacation times, and when student loans are released. </div> </div> </div>How does this equate to the basic economics of Gen Xers, as a demographic, having more disposable income than Mllenials and Zoomers to right now? How does timing your biggest release for mid-August help with that (since Paradox insist on corebooks getting done for Gen Con).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, great discussion dude, glad we can have it without yelling and screaming and cursing at each other </div> </div> </div>We're old, we shouldn't tempt fate. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T02:24:28-07:00","id":1520863,"title":"","content":"For the record I think the writters are 'woke' it's more that woke is a pretty vague term and quite subjective (having been called an alt right chud and a series of expletives interlacted with femminist for the same stance indicates flexibility on the subject.,) individually the average WoD writter so is woke I'm suprised their eyes don't glue blue and they show up on a sandworm, some parts of w5 make me cringe with how twitter preachy they are. However the company itself is corporate woke which is &quot;make money of minorities while avoiding controversy&quot; which combined with other factors creates a sense of false wokeness.<br /> <br /> edit-to say nothing of your personal politics doesn't exactly equate to sound judgement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-18-2023, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T14:54:24-07:00","id":1520901,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1520860]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've had multiple creatives and community volunteers come forward (since before V5 was even in alpha test state) pointing out that no, it's just pandering and no they're not trying to do more than pander and manage PR. Some of the authors most certain have tried, but they're the one's Paradox have driven off. </div> </div> </div>I'm personally hesitant to take words at face value. There are many that will argue that no one does enough. Thats not to dismiss pandering. That certainly is a factor. I think Paradox is falling victim to &quot;old man syndrome&quot;, meaning that someone points out a potential issue, and they brush it off saying &quot;you're over-reacting, there's no way that'll be an issue&quot; and, well, folks love to say I told you so. Such is the nature of the internet. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You kinda do, because anecdote isn't data. One of the stores around here has a first printing V5 core hard copy at 25% off and nobody's bothered buying it, let alone asked for more stock to get ordered. </div> </div> </div>That book is still a sold unit. It has been purchased by the store with the store ordering, 1, 10 or 1000 on the expectation that they'll sell them. Maybe your store ordered too many. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, there's a simple explanation beyond how much living in a small town rural area means local group preferences which are by no means indicative of the whole audience in the world skews things: too many of us order our stuff online because our public transit sucks and none of the stores that sell TTRPG books can afford big enough spaces towards things like having play areas in the store to build a community around. Why try to find ~1 hr of time to get to a store, maybe more to try out the second, and plenty of gas money to go along with it, when it can just arrive on my doorstep and the shipping doesn't feel so bad compared to when gas was cheaper and I had way more free time. </div> </div> </div>I kinda miss going to brick and mortar but I'm far too lazy, and I like shit showing up at my door for the same reasons you listed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that the bad press has pretty much been on Paradox's shoulders for demands they're making of studios (plus plenty of dumb things they've said in response t various PR issues). Modiphus was dropped as what seems to be more of a business incompatibility with distribution than content (since Paradox was still doing most of the content then, and was heavily involved in the few books Modiphius did. The only controversies with Onyx Path were things like the entire W20 team at Onyx Path giving up on new books until Apocalyptic Record because they were tired of Paradox forcing them to put in bad content. None of the Hunter's Entertainment books were particularly controversial, but we've heard a lot about how much tension there was because that team wanted H5 and W5 to be more like V5 (be an update and continuation of the older game instead of a full reboot). Though Sambrano's treatment while a member of the Hunter's W5 team is another PR blunder complete on Paradox's shoulders. Epic - like Onyx Path for that matter - hasn't been &quot;dropped&quot; as much as not offered any new jobs because Epic's only contributions to the TTRPG books is based on their video game. And Renegade is the current primary WoD5 partner studio. </div> </div> </div>Modiphius got slammed with that scandal on release with the Brujah drama and iirc the MRH piece not to mention the blog on release, that I don't want to publicly talk about. As I recall there was the one mag that trashed vtm as a whole for some crap. It seemed like daily there was a new drama. Then Onyx Path had some crap over nothing, though I wish OP was just handed everything, cause those folks are fans of the franchise, and steadily put out quality.<br /> I missed the Sambrano stuff, so I'm not familiar, and can't comment on it. I don't mind Renegade, but It seems like they are pushing the board games more than the TT game. Maybe thats just me. Perhaps its doing well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of this though, is about the health of the brand as a whole. Paradox didn't buy the WoD to just build up a TTRPG brand from the small audience it held onto under Onyx Path's care, they want an expanded media brand. That's their stated goal in all this. So that media needs to actually be putting a dent in those markets; which is really hard when there isn't even anything new to put out for a lot of them. These things are how Paradox really things the brand will grow. The TTRPGs are like Marvel still making comics even though there are individual MCU movies that made more money than comic books sales have in multiple years: completely abandoning the legacy media form the brand started in would be horrible marketing, but it's not where there's real growth to be had. </div> </div> </div>I think Paradox bought WoD in anticipation of it gaining a significant portion of their former glory, as D&amp;D did. I think its holding its own but not hitting near the numbers of the 90s<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the more successful indie devs once broke down the numbers for folks and showed that in practical buying power (that is, not raw dollar amounts) the size of the RPG market has been stagnant since the 2000s recession. Even with all the increased D&amp;D popularity of the last few years, TTRPG books themselves haven't seen any serious increase in how much the general audience is spending relative to things like the costs of production. TTRPG can, basically, only really grow by taking customers from other TTRPGs. Other markets are where there's actual room for growth instead of fighting over how big of a slice of the pie you get is. </div> </div> </div>But did they account for digital sales? Thats a common tactic in the music industry, to discuss the physical units while ignoring digital sales The music industry, and now the film industry are all trying to figure out how that works, but I have no idea where books fall into in that mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't have it both ways. Either you are speaking for folks (because you're claiming the entire fanbase is saying specific things), or you're not talkin about the actual vocal fanbase, you're just cherry-picking individual posts.<br /> <br /> A lot of what you're seeing isn't hypocrisy as much as this fanbase not actually being nearly as unified about a lot of things as yous seem to think. </div> </div> </div>All I can speak to is what I see, though to be fair, habitually, those that are happy with a product tend to chime in a lot less than those that have complaints. But looking at this very thread, the first couple of comments are &quot;I hate v5.&quot; I don't think folks are unified. I think like I said on my last comment, that I think everyone wants the game designed specifically for their table, and no company can do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because Paradox doesn't have any idea of what realistically &quot;winning&quot; in the TTRPG space looks like. They're doing... basically what you're doing: taking these really shallow reads of fan reactions, and instead of trying to deep dive into what's really going on, they're just reacting to the surface level stuff. Of course that's a no-win strategy. And if they actually listened more thoroughly, they'd have a much better idea of how to avoid the constant PR problems they keep having. </div> </div> </div>agreed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That was 19 years ago. The conversation has moved on. </div> </div> </div>Yet its still the same. replace CoD with v5 and its almost identical<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BJD wasn't the first V5 book, it was the last V20 book. That's one of the reasons it's actually better at getting older fans and newer fans to talk about lore deep dives than V5 core is. </div> </div> </div>I mean, one could argue it either way, I'm not ready to die on that hill. V20.5? I agree it was a great bridge but if one looks at it like a v5 book, there is like 500 pages of metaplot for people to use!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While having Outstar be a big public face of the company helps it look younger, the head WoD folks for Paradox have generally been of the older and mid Gen Xers in age range. It's not being run by a whole new generation of folks coming to this with fresh eyes. It's being run by folks that were into it back in the 90s too.<br /> <br /> All three WoD5 core books so far have been worked on by people that worked on TTRPG for the old WW back in the day. The keys didn't get passed on to your grandchildren, they got sold to someone about your age (maybe a few years younger) because that car was cool back in the day to them too, and they're hoping a good paint job can make it cool again to the actual younger generation. </div> </div> </div>My players range from 40s- early/mid 20s. I'm seeing plenty of kids 19+ looking for games online. Kids that literally could be my kids (and not having it be too weird) otherwise I concede to your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It feels like you're conflating at least to separate things (The need for WoD to adapt to the times, and whether or not V5 did that well). </div> </div> </div>I think they are both kind of the same thing. Vtm has always been the flagship of the WoD, you can't discuss the one without the other. Statistically, Vtm <i>should</i> have the most missteps, as its the first one. With WtA it seems they overcompensated in the opposite direction in some cases for better or worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it didn't. And to actually make a case instead of assert my feelings as facts: Jason Car (the one that works for Paradox as a brand manager!)l, who runs one of the more popular live-plays for V5, basically doesn't use the books because he ended up using so many house rules and setting homebrew that people actually started complaining that the book they bought didn't seem to be the game he was running.<br /> <br /> If one of the company's top PR folks has to very liberally apply the Golden Rule to make the game functional for live streaming him running it for a group, that's a really big indicator that it did not do a great job.<br /> <br /> It means it has potential, but one I've sen Paradox consistently squander instead of treasure. </div> </div> </div>We all customize rules for our own table. in 2nd ed D&amp;D did we use every single rule? no. The job of a rpg designer is to create the framework, and give direction as to intent as if they tried to use every rule or make a rule for every circumstance the books become so rule heavy that its no longer fun. Plus (speaking for myself, but I'll bet money that most others feel the same) I have a life. I have to remember tax laws, work visa laws etc etc. As adults we have so much to remember, and this game already takes up a huge amount of mental bandwidth that I feel like its in bad faith to assume he or any storyteller uses the golden rule because the game is broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure I'd rather have the VtM edition Rich and Eddy were working on to pitch to CCP before the Paradox buy out. No, it wouldn't have been perfect, it wouldn't appeal to everyone, but I'm fairly confident it would have done all the good things V5 did, but better, and with a much smaller set of major missteps to deal with. </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. I think that would have huge potential to go either way...at least I'd recognize the authors....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe read past that? Because there's a lot more being discussed than that. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. That shit just pisses me off. And I'm personally just happy the brand is still here, so I can use new books instead of my beat up 90s collection<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Right. It's not just about targeting the new fans and leaving us grognards to either get on board of hoard our old books. </div> </div> </div>In a perfect world they'd get both, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does this equate to the basic economics of Gen Xers, as a demographic, having more disposable income than Mllenials and Zoomers to right now? How does timing your biggest release for mid-August help with that (since Paradox insist on corebooks getting done for Gen Con). </div> </div> </div>Easy - to hit one of the biggest marketing platforms of the gaming year. In music there are summer festivals. You generally make less playing those fests, and sell significantly less merch BUT you play them to be on the same bill as bigger artists, and to play on front of exponentially more folks than you would on your own in the hopes of picking up more fans. Fall and Spring are the busy seasons tho to get that sweet sweet student loan cash.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're old, we shouldn't tempt fate. :P </div> </div> </div>Yet here we are lol<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T15:01:02-07:00","id":1520902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520863#post1520863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record I think the writters are 'woke' it's more that woke is a pretty vague term and quite subjective (having been called an alt right chud and a series of expletives interlacted with femminist for the same stance indicates flexibility on the subject.,) individually the average WoD writter so is woke I'm suprised their eyes don't glue blue and they show up on a sandworm, some parts of w5 make me cringe with how twitter preachy they are. However the company itself is corporate woke which is &quot;make money of minorities while avoiding controversy&quot; which combined with other factors creates a sense of false wokeness.<br /> <br /> edit-to say nothing of your personal politics doesn't exactly equate to sound judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it has lost its meaning. And Twitter......well....thats a place...<br /> <br /> Staying politically neutral is a smart business practice. Try to piss off the least amount of people as possible. The writers, however, are independent and are free to hold whatever view they wish, and shout it from the rooftops the only risk is they lose a contract or be not considered for one (which they wouldn't even know)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T15:23:34-07:00","id":1520904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520901#post1520901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps. That shit just pisses me off. And I'm personally just happy the brand is still here, so I can use new books instead of my beat up 90s collection</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two things are going to make for vastly different experiences. For all its faults, old W:tA never read like a Black Spiral Dancer was writing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a perfect world they'd get both, right?<br /> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't even need to be perfect. There were glaring things that needed to be fixed in W:tA; what got altered was largely not counted among them, and it wasn't even really a fix. You can still see where they painted over the brand manager's intent to have the Swords of Heimdall take over the Get of Fenris (in spite of the latter having killed the members of the former over 20 years ago) in how it claims that the Cult of Fenris and anyone who falls to Hauglosk is an extremist that teeters on &quot;ecofascism&quot;, in spite of the text not showing an indicating of understanding what that word actually means.<br /> <br /> There were so many modest actions that could be taken, so many things that would have occurred to any W:tA veteran, but apparently the brand manager is so deep into the weeds of Vampire that &quot;fix problems with other WoD games&quot; translates to him as &quot;make other WoD games almost exactly like a reskinned Vampire, cut out as much as possible to make it happen&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T02:26:29-07:00","id":1521017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520786#post1520786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wouldn't give Paradox too much credit for the STV. I'd bet a considerable amount of money on that happening regardless (mostly because OBS, the company that runs DTRPG and all those community content services like STV, is owned by one of the original WW founders and even during the CCP days that lead to a close relationship between the people making the games and getting into those outlets).</div> </div> </div> </div>We should give due credit to Martin Ericsson, when he announced the STV I still remember it was met with the usual ridicule in these discussions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Paradox achieving a profit out of the deal, I think their last year financial documents didn't show amortization costs connected to the WW buyout, so either it was somewhere else, or they have already got to break even","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 08-20-2023, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T02:33:51-07:00","id":1521018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evolved_lupus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520833#post1520833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Two can play this game: THEY need to accept the fact that in the 2020s, as opposed to the 1990s, WE receive more information about their products before they hit the shelves (digital or otherwise) and, based upon this info, we can choose to simply not purchase said products, therefore depriving them of cash, ruining their profit projections and turning certain hits into unexpected flops. Will it kill WoD5? Uncertain, but possible. Will it prevent WoD5 contending with D&amp;D for the title of &quot;Number One RPG&quot; like in the 1990s due to the fanbase being overly fractured? Most definitely.</span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So far both Icv2 and Drivethru charts show WoD5e in comparatively good health; they are not contending the Number One title, but they are among the top 10 tier, and have shown the capacity to reach top 5 positions; which, for a small team not into the supplement thread mills model, is enough to sustain the business","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T04:53:56-07:00","id":1521024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521017#post1521017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should give due credit to Martin Ericsson, when he announced the STV I still remember it was met with the usual ridicule in these discussions</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to check your memory. The idea of the STV wasn't ridiculed, the timing, implementation, and limited material was ridiculed.<br /> <br /> Important context:<br /> <br /> 1) The STV launched <b>before</b> V5 was actually published, and only allowed VtM's first for modern nights editions. No other WoD gamelines, the CofD, or Exalted were allowed. No past lines like Dark Ages or Victorian Era Vampire were allowed. You could publish limited content for three editions, the most recent of which had been cancelled over a decade before, or the more recent edition which already had a very thorough set of supplements.<br /> <br /> 2) The launch was during the height of the PR disaster that was hiring Zak S and then declaring him innocent based on an &quot;investigation&quot; done by nWW. A lot of people that wanted to use the STV were very unhappy with the idea that their work might be putting money in Zak's pockets because nWW hadn't fully committed to never hiring him again yet.<br /> <br /> 3) There was also, esp. in the existing community of fan supplement makers before this that operated on the Dark Pack rules, a large amount of distrust towards nWW because their revision of the Dark Pack fan material rule had massive legal problems, and the promise to address and clarify this by establishing different rules for different kind of fan materials was never actually finished (and this is actually still in place for anything like a fan website, blog, or forum about the games). CofD and Exalted inclusive fan-sites had to reject using the Dark Pack license because the approved art assets (including logos, icons, and so on) weren't included for those games (and still aren't).<br /> <br /> 4) And of course, all the dumb shit Martin said because he vastly overestimated his communication skills in English, and generally let himself ramble in any language far more than a person in his former position should specifically because of all the PR gaffes he made.<br /> <br /> So yes, there was ridicule. But it wasn't because people hated the idea. It was because Paradox and nWW hadn't actually done anything to earn an iota of goodwill from the people that would want to put content in it, and were justifiably worried about promises being made to expand the STV into what it should have been at launch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Paradox achieving a profit out of the deal, I think their last year financial documents didn't show amortization costs connected to the WW buyout, so either it was somewhere else, or they have already got to break even </div> </div> </div>I've looked at all of their public end of year reports since the buyout. They've never mentioned the amortization of the buyout. They barely even mentioned the buyout itself. Reading between the lines, the WW IPs are lumped in with only their accountants know what else in a general investment section where they talk about reassessing and evaluating the financial risks and rewards of their smaller acquisitions and other investments. This is very consistent with both them not breaking even yet, and the rather frequent changes we've seen in their efforts to monetize the buyout.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521018#post1521018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far both Icv2 and Drivethru charts show WoD5e in comparatively good health; they are not contending the Number One title, but they are among the top 10 tier, and have shown the capacity to reach top 5 positions; which, for a small team not into the supplement thread mills model, is enough to sustain the business</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh.<br /> <br /> So, for the whatever number time this is:<br /> <br /> Sales is not the same thing has health. If Company A sells a million books for a gross profit of $5 million, but production, distribution, employee compensation, and marketting all cost $7.5 million, while Company B grossed $75K on something that cost them $50K to make, Company B despite the much lower sales, is actually making a profit, while Company A is bleeding themselves out.<br /> <br /> Also, Paradox 's WoD team is not a &quot;small&quot; operation by TTRPG standards. Just based on who's listed as an employee and not a freelancer, they're easily in the top 10 companies in terms of employees that work on making TTRPGs when you take into account they're just working on the WoD. And that's despite how much they license off to other studios. Chaosium and Green Ronin have less employees working for their entire companies, than Paradox has working on just the WoD. WotC and Paizo are the only companies that have pubic listings of over 50 people just working on their TTRPGs. All of what feel like &quot;big names&quot; that make up the &quot;medium&quot; sized TTRPG studios are between 10-15 employees, and even most are like Onyx Path with less than 5 full employees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T09:13:54-07:00","id":1521035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520831#post1520831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna say something super dramatic/controversial (though correct):<br /> <br /> V5 is bloody great<br /> The &quot;woke shit&quot; is here to stay, like it or not.<br /> Vampire brings in plenty of money and is growing as a brand.<br /> They got rid of the meta plot because WE bitched and bitched claiming we hate it.<br /> WE said the only good thing about CoD was the ruleset, so they used a bunch of it.<br /> WE made the Sabbat one dimensional powergamey murderhobos so they had to take it away, that way the entire line doesn't get painted by those that prefer that style of gameplay.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself, I loved the metaplot. Didn't really play cod outside of changeling. and tend to have a low opinion of people who thumb their noses down at combat orientated games even though I don't play them (as though amateur theatrics is somehow more meaningful).<br /> <br /> If their is a error its that I and other fans didn't bite back because we were happy so all white wolf got was the sort of people who thought the lasombra should be in the carmarilla because they're snazzy dressers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T10:46:19-07:00","id":1521043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521024#post1521024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sales is not the same thing has health. If Company A sells a million books for a gross profit of $5 million, but production, distribution, employee compensation, and marketting all cost $7.5 million, while Company B grossed $75K on something that cost them $50K to make, Company B despite the much lower sales, is actually making a profit, while Company A is bleeding themselves out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is obvious, but still, if Wod5 enters the icv charts for almost a year by now, based on mostly reprints of manuals which were financed by crowdfunding some years ago, I'd say that their cut on profits in the last months is probably satisfactory<br /> <br /> Also, an interesting part of V5 sales are also international, as Paradox has a much wider set of localization agreements, and even though those are not direct profits, they are still widely distributed revenues, with no attached entrepreneurial risk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:12:52-07:00","id":1521057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521043#post1521043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is obvious, but still, if Wod5 enters the icv charts for almost a year by now, based on mostly reprints of manuals which were financed by crowdfunding some years ago, I'd say that their cut on profits in the last months is probably satisfactory<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, we cannot know that since we don't have any data on the cost of production+ the employee's salaries+ the terms of contracts with other studio, etc<br /> <br /> As far as we know, V5 could be a success or the biggest money pit in TTRPG history. We cannot know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T15:28:55-07:00","id":1521078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521043#post1521043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is obvious, but still,...</div> </div> </div> </div>No &quot;but still.&quot; If this is obvious, than just citing the ICv2 surveys of retailers is obviously insufficient for the claims your making.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if Wod5 enters the icv charts for almost a year by now, based on mostly reprints of manuals which were financed by crowdfunding some years ago, I'd say that their cut on profits in the last months is probably satisfactory </div> </div> </div>The only books that were crowdfunded for V5 were the ones made by Onyx Path (traditional preorders are not crowdfunding, and are not transparent), and some of the localization studios. It's impossible for those to be holding up the line on their own.<br /> <br /> Lets do a quick gut check here. To be conservative, let's say Paradox compensates (that is, the total outlay of the company including compensations and benefits beyond salary) the equivalent of $50K annually to ten employees (there are more than that, but their salaries aren't published and the specifics aren't public, and there's been turnover, etc.). That's $500K, a year, for the last seven years. If Paradox nets $5 per sale, they need to sell 100K books a year, just to pay their WoD staff (oh, and they didn't actually have anything to sell for the first two years). Now, fortunately for Paradox, they decided to offload a lot of one-time costs associated with RPs onto their production partners. Paradox doesn't pay the freelance writers, artists, editors, and consultants, Renegade/whoever does (but that's also why Paradox makes less per book, because Renegade needs a bigger cut to stay profitable on their side of things).<br /> <br /> And, of course, the estimates I saw was that Paradox paid about $4 million for the buyout. At $5 per book, that's... 800K more book sales to break even. That would man V5 is selling books on par with D&amp;D 5e, or they're still not breaking even. Since WoD5 has ranged from not place in the ICv2 top 5, to 4th place at best, it isn't out selling Pathfinder/Paizo, so it isn't doing D&amp;D numbers, so it hasn't broken even yet. Yes, they're also trickling in small things like licensing fees from their various business partners, but Onyx Path's payments to keep making Exalted is chump change in these sorts of equations, or Rich couldn't afford to do it.<br /> <br /> And I haven' even tried to account for things like the development hell of Bloodlines 2 and how much money got poured into the marketing hype for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, an interesting part of V5 sales are also international, as Paradox has a much wider set of localization agreements, and even though those are not direct profits, they are still widely distributed revenues, with no attached entrepreneurial risk </div> </div> </div>If there was no risk, everyone would be doing it.<br /> <br /> Want to know why most RPGs don't bother with that? It costs too much. Remember that English is already the most widely spoken language on Earth. After English and Mandarin, the number of speakers (both native and secondary) of any language drops by a huge margin. For physical books, which are already a slim profit margin product, localization into more specific language markets is threading a very tough needle: You need to have extremely good estimates of what each language's market is for localization is over how many gamers gave up ages ago and speak enough English to run TTRPGs out of the standard English text; or at least have enough people in their group that can parse the technical rules parts of it. Otherwise you have no idea what kind of print runs to be aiming for, and localization companies aren't set up to do that kind of market research.<br /> <br /> So, you can put a lot of money into researching individual language markets, localization partners, and also still have to work on distribution of physical product..aka have risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T02:53:01-07:00","id":1521112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521057#post1521057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, we cannot know that since we don't have any data on the cost of production+ the employee's salaries+ the terms of contracts with other studio, etc<br /> <br /> As far as we know, V5 could be a success or the biggest money pit in TTRPG history. We cannot know</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside success as a gaming system and achieving progress in regard to sales and popularity, I think that it definitely does matter that V5 and subsquent VtM supplements and books are an authentic and honest attempt in creating a setting, descriptions, and stories.<br /> <br /> Role playing games ( and other mediums and works, like card games ) are kept afloat and expanded to a considerable extent thanks to a well written and drawn fictional world and authentic characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T09:53:57-07:00","id":1521134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520831#post1520831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna say something super dramatic/controversial (though correct):<br /> <br /> V5 is bloody great<br /> The &quot;woke shit&quot; is here to stay, like it or not.<br /> Vampire brings in plenty of money and is growing as a brand.<br /> They got rid of the meta plot because WE bitched and bitched claiming we hate it.<br /> WE said the only good thing about CoD was the ruleset, so they used a bunch of it.<br /> WE made the Sabbat one dimensional powergamey murderhobos so they had to take it away, that way the entire line doesn't get painted by those that prefer that style of gameplay.<br /> <br /> Thats not to say, Onyx Path and Paradox haven't stumbled here and there, but all in all they modernized a product that we have been circle jerking over for the last 20 years and brought us into the 2020s and <b><i>marketing to new fans with modern sensibilities</i></b>.<br /> We need to accept that what was acceptable in 1990 is not acceptable in 2020 (shocker, I know).<br /> The times has evolved, and the brand evolved with it. They aren't marketing to us old timers. We have less time, and less disposable income.<br /> <br /> V6 (if it happens) will continue this trend. The social landscape has been evolving quickly even, since the launch of V5, to the point that in the time it takes to write, edit, print, and distribute a book, things have changed. This is affecting all areas of entertainment, from movies to TV to music, video games etc etc. The Vault is incredible and allows us as a community to get work out there, faster than Paradox can market to the world.<br /> <br /> I think V6 will happen in 5-10 years and will likely be more directed towards online use, since it seems that the majority of games take place online.<br /> <br /> Cheers, and back into my hole where I'll continue to play with a bunch of old people and a couple of babies ;P</div> </div> </div> </div>They did not bring CoD ruleset, Vampire the Requiem &quot;2nd ED&quot; is fine oiled machine whose power levels can get even bigger than the revised era with multiple alternate rules to support all kind of games (they are called tiers), furthermore homebrewing is heavily encouraged as everything is modular, you get a ton of option to modify the vainilla game to your liking.<br /> <br /> On the other hand V5 has a rigid anti-system that takes away freedom from players and Game masters, the mechanics are so interwined that you cannot barely touch one without affecting others, not to mention the system is made to force the players to play in the true way of having fun (irony), where players cannot controls their characters as hunger dice and compulsions take away their agency by &quot;raw rules&quot; making all vampires disfuntional predators. Not to mention some banes making a lot of clans unplayable and undefined mechanics, there is a point where the core asks &quot;How fast is fast&quot; and it does not provide an actual answer.<br /> <br /> The comparision is unfair V5 is a car with an engine that works according to your horoscope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T13:51:39-07:00","id":1521149,"title":"","content":"So how many copies of a particular gaming book does a company need to sell before it's considered a successful endenaver? (Excuse the spelling with the more fancier words I might use from time to time)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T15:00:26-07:00","id":1521152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521149#post1521149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how many copies of a particular gaming book does a company need to sell before it's considered a successful endenaver? (Excuse the spelling with the more fancier words I might use from time to time)</div> </div> </div> </div>By Big Company Standards? WotC/Hasbro has something like <u>3 million</u> copies of the 5e PHB in circulation, half of them sold, and management considered that &quot;under-monetized&quot;. Supplements were usually a third of that, at best, to a tenth of that. So, for a core, a whole fucking lot, if you want to re-live the glory days of the 90s when Vampire was just behind AD&amp;D 2e. Which definitely isn't happening, because you wouldn't be able to not hear about it if it had. Paradox would be screaming it out to anyone who was listening and there would be many, many YouTube videos about how all manner of people love V5 and why.<br /> <br /> But it's a likely very distant 4th or 5th, at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T15:03:48-07:00","id":1521153,"title":"","content":"There is no magic number, because success is a factor of net profits, not gross sales. A book that costs $20K to make needs to sell less copies to turn a profit than a book that costs $40K to make.<br /> <br /> For a company, there's also a consistency of sales. One mega hit book that sells a lot of copies, but the company can't replicate in new releases, means the company can't sustain itself, while a company that never has any giant hits, but consistently sells OK over many books can keep going until something big happens externally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T16:24:44-07:00","id":1521155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521152#post1521152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...But it's a likely very distant 4th or 5th, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just moved back into the top 5 as of the last published ivc2 numbers for Fall of 2022. Prior to that V5 had been in the 4th spot twice (Spring and Summer 2019) and 5th spot of Vampire (still listed under White Wolf) Fall 2018. I wouldn\u2019t be able to explain the sudden appearance at the 4 spot, no V5 books were released it that time frame unless they include H5, unless maybe that\u2019s when Renegade got around to releasing their edited version of Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> Full Data - <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/wiki/top_rpgs/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.enworld.org/wiki/top_rpgs/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T07:42:05-07:00","id":1521186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520786#post1520786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going &quot;open source&quot; would be a giant dick-punch to Onyx Path considering that would destroy their ability to make money off of Exalted in the process..</div> </div> </div> </div>They could create their own entirely separate World of Darkness continuity.<br /> <br /> Sort of like Damnation City.<br /> <br /> And it would be awesome to give them free reign with the characters like Beckett, Lucita, and others the main line has no interest developing.<br /> <br /> Do a V6 baed on what they were planning to do with BECKETT'S JYHAD DIARY.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T07:43:59-07:00","id":1521187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1520831#post1520831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna say something super dramatic/controversial (though correct):<br /> <br /> V5 is bloody great<br /> The &quot;woke shit&quot; is here to stay, like it or not.<br /> Vampire brings in plenty of money and is growing as a brand.<br /> They got rid of the meta plot because WE bitched and bitched claiming we hate it.<br /> WE said the only good thing about CoD was the ruleset, so they used a bunch of it.<br /> WE made the Sabbat one dimensional powergamey murderhobos so they had to take it away, that way the entire line doesn't get painted by those that prefer that style of gameplay.<br /> <br /> Thats not to say, Onyx Path and Paradox haven't stumbled here and there, but all in all they modernized a product that we have been circle jerking over for the last 20 years and brought us into the 2020s and <b><i>marketing to new fans with modern sensibilities</i></b>.<br /> We need to accept that what was acceptable in 1990 is not acceptable in 2020 (shocker, I know).<br /> The times has evolved, and the brand evolved with it. They aren't marketing to us old timers. We have less time, and less disposable income.<br /> <br /> V6 (if it happens) will continue this trend. The social landscape has been evolving quickly even, since the launch of V5, to the point that in the time it takes to write, edit, print, and distribute a book, things have changed. This is affecting all areas of entertainment, from movies to TV to music, video games etc etc. The Vault is incredible and allows us as a community to get work out there, faster than Paradox can market to the world.<br /> <br /> I think V6 will happen in 5-10 years and will likely be more directed towards online use, since it seems that the majority of games take place online.<br /> <br /> Cheers, and back into my hole where I'll continue to play with a bunch of old people and a couple of babies ;P</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused at the idea anyone can be a vampire fan and worry about &quot;wokeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a fucking counter-culture PUNK game.<br /> <br /> Hating capitalism, loving minorities, and being accepting of everyone while being pissed off about the state of the world is baked into its DNA.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night 1st Edition was the most diverse RPG supplement of all time for races, cultures, sexual identities, and other stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T08:08:36-07:00","id":1521188,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the new games aren't really particularly &quot;woke&quot;. They seek to be hip without actually being political or philosophical hoping to leave that out of the game as it might cause controversy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T10:28:38-07:00","id":1521201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521187#post1521187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused at the idea anyone can be a vampire fan and worry about &quot;wokeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a fucking counter-culture PUNK game.<br /> <br /> Hating capitalism, loving minorities, and being accepting of everyone while being pissed off about the state of the world is baked into its DNA.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night 1st Edition was the most diverse RPG supplement of all time for races, cultures, sexual identities, and other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is the world has moved on what it means to be counter-cultural has too. Most was what was counter-cultural in the 90\u2019s is the mainstream today. The disaffected of today aren\u2019t the disaffected then.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not PUNK or counter-culture to put a rainbow flag on your Twitter header and come out in support of the Trans movement when the government, the corporations and the media (all of whom are in bed together to rob the working classes) are threatening jail time for those in opposition.<br /> <br /> Its flacid mass market drivel you can find anywhere on Netflix, Max, Disney+ and kiddy shows.<br /> <br /> The 90\u2019s punks and all their agendas have become The Man, only they wanna pretend they\u2019re still the punks. They\u2019re not and so it feels inauthentic. They can\u2019t present genuine punk viewpoints because if you\u2019re The Man then the punks have to be stupid and wrong or even criminal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T11:12:39-07:00","id":1521205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521186#post1521186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could create their own entirely separate World of Darkness continuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>So could anyone else. That's the whole problem for Onyx Path if Paradox did something like make the WoD into an open license property. Onyx Path's profits for these products are built on a level of exclusivity. They aren't Paradox, but they get to make official books, that are part of the official continuity. If you take that away, Onyx Path could still sell books (because Onyx Path is still the most trusted company when it comes to doing the WoD games well), but suddenly Onyx Path has to compete with lots and lots of other publishers. It's the 3.0 OGL boom and bust all over, but Onyx Path has way less money in the bank to endure it and then try to be the WoD's Paizo once the dust settles.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring up Exalted, is because that's the one place where Onyx Path really is the only company that can do it; even if they don't own the IP. Unless you want to piss off a lot of Exalted fans by cancelling 3e early and then starting a brand new edition (and the devs who's work you'd be cancelling are part of the small cadre of people that actually know how to make Exalted, and they're part of those fans you'd be pissing off). Unless there's some pretty significant changes in the current state of things, there's no Exalted without Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> If you make the system open, and suddenly there's a dozen version of, &quot;If I was in charge of Exalted Essence, here's what I would have done,&quot; flooding the market... you're just driving Onyx Path to stop paying Paradox license fees and focus even more on the various Storypath games. Onyx Path has had a lot of time to build up those properties and not be reliant on Paradox like they used to be completely at the whim of CCP.<br /> <br /> Whatever your ideal situation here might be, the reality would by that Onyx Path as a company just moves on, while some Onyx Path freelancers try to use their name recognition in the fandom to put out some books of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T11:13:15-07:00","id":1521206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521201#post1521201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is the world has moved on what it means to be counter-cultural has too. Most was what was counter-cultural in the 90\u2019s is the mainstream today. The disaffected of today aren\u2019t the disaffected then.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not PUNK or counter-culture to put a rainbow flag on your Twitter header and come out in support of the Trans movement when the government, the corporations and the media (all of whom are in bed together to rob the working classes) are threatening jail time for those in opposition.<br /> <br /> Its flacid mass market drivel you can find anywhere on Netflix, Max, Disney+ and kiddy shows.<br /> <br /> The 90\u2019s punks and all their agendas have become The Man, only they wanna pretend they\u2019re still the punks. They\u2019re not and so it feels inauthentic. They can\u2019t present genuine punk viewpoints because if you\u2019re The Man then the punks have to be stupid and wrong or even criminal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truer words have never been spoken, and I say this as someone who is LGBTQ and has several pride flags at my house and on my online profiles. I'm sick of the pandering from these corporations. It's very patronizing and insulting.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, I also used to consider myself a far-leftist until fairly late into 2020 when I had a severe mental breakdown after years of being subject to a very extreme degree of gaslighting, extortion, abuse, constant purity spirals and struggle sessions, and tyranny within that movement. <br /> <br /> Here's the kicker to all this...Most of the bigwig corporate stiffs on Wall Street and Silicon Valley nowadays are Generation X'ers, as opposed to the stereotypical country club Boomer in a fancy suit (most of those types of guys are retired now)<br /> <br /> And most of those modern Gen X corporate execs and traders were the goths, punks, and alternative kids of the 80's, 90's, and early 2000's all grown up now. The punks of that era were more often intellectuals at heart and the more cutthroat and entrepreneurial Gen X punks did their best to worm their way into finance and tech.<br /> <br /> Those punks and goths of the old days now are a bunch of corporatist neoliberals, neoconservatives, and neo-feudalists who are LARP'ing as progressives and anarchists to dupe the masses and to convince themselves they're still radical punks rebelling against The Man instead of admitting that they are The Man now.<br /> <br /> It's irony at its absolute finest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T12:17:25-07:00","id":1521211,"title":"","content":"Eh....<br /> <br /> I think people forget that Gen-X wasn't all that progressive, punk, goth, or whatever. Those were still subcultures and counter cultures. Int he early 90s New Kids on the Block as the biggest thing, not Rage Against the Machine, or Nirvana, or even Green Day. Go watch PCU and Clueless, and after you stop being distracted by what Paul Rudd looked like almost 30 years ago compared to now, realize the that the mainstream characters were a mockery of what most early 90s teens were like. They were yuppies expecting to ride high on Reaganomics, and the promise of material wealth via the awesomeness of Capitalism. They grew up with the fall of the USSR proving 'Murica and money are the best. Skaters, college/alt rockers, feminists, etc. were all the butts of jokes, not the cool kids. Most of Gen-X was, and still is, pretty damned conservative by US standards,<br /> <br /> Being edgy is always appealing though. So as Gen-X grew up, a lot of them thought having a few CDs that were breakout hits of subcultures in their boy band and mall queen collections meant they were really into those things as kids too. Just like Boomer yuppies before them, they bought counter-culture couture made by brands the real counter culture hated, thought listening to the most pop-friendly sliver of uncool music was hip, and drank the nostalgia-aid into thinking they were down with the cause back in the day when really they just wanted to know a decent drug dealer.<br /> <br /> There's the people that say things like they don't remember Pearl Jam being &quot;political&quot; when they were kids (just like people don't &quot;remember&quot; Bruce Springsteen being &quot;political&quot; too) because they tossed on 10 to be pretentious, not give a shit about the lyrics.<br /> <br /> Sure, some punks and grunge kids, and so on hopped on the yuppie bandwagon later in life... but the yuppies were the majority the whole time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T12:33:51-07:00","id":1521213,"title":"","content":"Ok Imma reply to a bunch of shit in one post 'cause I'm lazy<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Going &quot;open source&quot; would be a giant dick-punch to Onyx Path considering that would destroy their ability to make money off of Exalted in the process..&quot;</b></i><br /> 100%. I think we agree more than we disagree<br /> <br /> Ok here's where it gets complicated<br /> <i><b>I'm confused at the idea anyone can be a vampire fan and worry about &quot;wokeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a fucking counter-culture PUNK game.</b></i><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> You're right, it WAS counter-culture punk game.<br /> <br /> however, define &quot;punk&quot; - Some would immediately say &quot;the Sex Pistols&quot; who were for all intents and purposes a corporate boy band.<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Hating capitalism, loving minorities, and being accepting of everyone while being pissed off about the state of the world is baked into its DNA.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night 1st Edition was the most diverse RPG supplement of all time for races, cultures, sexual identities, and other stuff.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Here's where it gets tricky. For in order to rail against it, it has to exist. As I recall, and correct me if I'm wrong, Mr Dawkins merely mentioned that a Brujah *could* be a nazi, can caught all sorts of hell for that. Therein lies the issue with &quot;wokeness&quot;, that I think people have a problem with. If a storyteller can't even paint the &quot;bad guy&quot;, how can they possibly write in the player defeating the &quot;man&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><i>&quot;Honestly, the new games aren't really particularly &quot;woke&quot;. They seek to be hip without actually being political or philosophical hoping to leave that out of the game as it might cause controversy.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> The new games are in a way being forced into a level of wokeness by a small but vocal minority, not to mention, through the eyes of 2015-2023, some things have become simply unacceptable that were totally acceptable in 1990.<br /> Otherwise, I agree<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;The thing is the world has moved on what it means to be counter-cultural has too. Most was what was counter-cultural in the 90\u2019s is the mainstream today. The disaffected of today aren\u2019t the disaffected then.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not PUNK or counter-culture to put a rainbow flag on your Twitter header and come out in support of the Trans movement when the government, the corporations and the media (all of whom are in bed together to rob the working classes) are threatening jail time for those in opposition.<br /> <br /> Its flacid mass market drivel you can find anywhere on Netflix, Max, Disney+ and kiddy shows.<br /> <br /> The 90\u2019s punks and all their agendas have become The Man, only they wanna pretend they\u2019re still the punks. They\u2019re not and so it feels inauthentic. They can\u2019t present genuine punk viewpoints because if you\u2019re The Man then the punks have to be stupid and wrong or even criminal.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> I agree. I saw a thing with the chick from the NRA where she said that the genuineness of the press was as offensive as calling Green Day punk. That joke was lost on all the suits in the room but I thought it was hilarious. Punk these days is kids in suburbia putting on a costume, unlike the lifestyle of the 70s and 80s, and posting on a message board. (Ironic, I know)<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;So could anyone else. That's the whole problem for Onyx Path if Paradox did something like make the WoD into an open license property. Onyx Path's profits for these products are built on a level of exclusivity. They aren't Paradox, but they get to make official books, that are part of the official continuity. If you take that away, Onyx Path could still sell books (because Onyx Path is still the most trusted company when it comes to doing the WoD games well), but suddenly Onyx Path has to compete with lots and lots of other publishers. It's the 3.0 OGL boom and bust all over, but Onyx Path has way less money in the bank to endure it and then try to be the WoD's Paizo once the dust settles.<br /> <br /> The reason I bring up Exalted, is because that's the one place where Onyx Path really is the only company that can do it; even if they don't own the IP. Unless you want to piss off a lot of Exalted fans by cancelling 3e early and then starting a brand new edition (and the devs who's work you'd be cancelling are part of the small cadre of people that actually know how to make Exalted, and they're part of those fans you'd be pissing off). Unless there's some pretty significant changes in the current state of things, there's no Exalted without Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> If you make the system open, and suddenly there's a dozen version of, &quot;If I was in charge of Exalted Essence, here's what I would have done,&quot; flooding the market... you're just driving Onyx Path to stop paying Paradox license fees and focus even more on the various Storypath games. Onyx Path has had a lot of time to build up those properties and not be reliant on Paradox like they used to be completely at the whim of CCP.<br /> <br /> Whatever your ideal situation here might be, the reality would by that Onyx Path as a company just moves on, while some Onyx Path freelancers try to use their name recognition in the fandom to put out some books of their own.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Again, I agree 100%<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Truer words have never been spoken, and I say this as someone who is LGBTQ and has several pride flags at my house and on my online profiles. I'm sick of the pandering from these corporations. It's very patronizing and insulting.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, I also used to consider myself a far-leftist until fairly late into 2020 when I had a severe mental breakdown after years of being subject to a very extreme degree of gaslighting, extortion, abuse, constant purity spirals and struggle sessions, and tyranny within that movement.<br /> <br /> Here's the kicker to all this...Most of the bigwig corporate stiffs on Wall Street and Silicon Valley nowadays are Generation X'ers, as opposed to the stereotypical country club Boomer in a fancy suit (most of those types of guys are retired now)<br /> <br /> And most of those modern Gen X corporate execs and traders were the goths, punks, and alternative kids of the 80's, 90's, and early 2000's all grown up now. The punks of that era were more often intellectuals at heart and the more cutthroat and entrepreneurial Gen X punks did their best to worm their way into finance and tech.<br /> <br /> Those punks and goths of the old days now are a bunch of corporatist neoliberals, neoconservatives, and neo-feudalists who are LARP'ing as progressives and anarchists to dupe the masses and to convince themselves they're still radical punks rebelling against The Man instead of admitting that they are The Man now.<br /> <br /> It's irony at its absolute finest.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Back in the 90s we were all about the individual. &quot;Let me be me&quot; Now it seems &quot;me&quot; must fit into a box for someone else to fight for, and feel better at night. Otherwise I completely agree. Fuck, I AM one of those dudes<br /> <br /> I want to slip back to the finances for a moment:<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn't necessarily need to make their money back right away on V5. They bought the brand like most companies do, to invest in the brand and hopefully grow it into an ultimately profitable venture. Record labels are built off of this methodology, fund the band, make the money back off of sale. If sales are lacking, are there signifiers of an upward trend? Online activity, good youtube analytics, well attended live shows etc? Is there a reason to continue investing in this brand? Its hard to say right now with the limited information we have. Has V5 been profitable? I'd hazard to guess yes. I have seen many requests for a second printing of CbN and CotBG, so that would indicate either folks don't know where to buy these books, or that they are indeed sold out. Since buying them without the V5 book would be rather pointless, I think it'd be safe to say that at least an equal number of those units have sold. So the question becomes &quot;what was the initial number?&quot; Who knows. And none of this accounts for illegally downloaded pdfs which the business also accounts for, and may show potential future positive returns.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T12:59:17-07:00","id":1521214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521211#post1521211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh....<br /> <br /> I think people forget that Gen-X wasn't all that progressive, punk, goth, or whatever. Those were still subcultures and counter cultures. Int he early 90s New Kids on the Block as the biggest thing, not Rage Against the Machine, or Nirvana, or even Green Day. Go watch PCU and Clueless, and after you stop being distracted by what Paul Rudd looked like almost 30 years ago compared to now, realize the that the mainstream characters were a mockery of what most early 90s teens were like. They were yuppies expecting to ride high on Reaganomics, and the promise of material wealth via the awesomeness of Capitalism. They grew up with the fall of the USSR proving 'Murica and money are the best. Skaters, college/alt rockers, feminists, etc. were all the butts of jokes, not the cool kids. Most of Gen-X was, and still is, pretty damned conservative by US standards,<br /> <br /> Being edgy is always appealing though. So as Gen-X grew up, a lot of them thought having a few CDs that were breakout hits of subcultures in their boy band and mall queen collections meant they were really into those things as kids too. Just like Boomer yuppies before them, they bought counter-culture couture made by brands the real counter culture hated, thought listening to the most pop-friendly sliver of uncool music was hip, and drank the nostalgia-aid into thinking they were down with the cause back in the day when really they just wanted to know a decent drug dealer.<br /> <br /> There's the people that say things like they don't remember Pearl Jam being &quot;political&quot; when they were kids (just like people don't &quot;remember&quot; Bruce Springsteen being &quot;political&quot; too) because they tossed on 10 to be pretentious, not give a shit about the lyrics.<br /> <br /> Sure, some punks and grunge kids, and so on hopped on the yuppie bandwagon later in life... but the yuppies were the majority the whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're aging yourself my friend hahaha!<br /> I think the 90s were the first time in a long time that we were free from fear. In the 80s we were all gonna get nuked by the Russians. In the 90s we had time to be depressed and hate ourselves and try to break free the machine. Til the end of the 90s where we one again were all gonna die cause of Y2K. It was a different time, but a fun one. But I resent hearing the music I grew up with in the local grocery store....<br /> Hot Topic was a real place! Not just a joke! All my cds had warnings on them! I went outside!!! <br /> <br /> Instead I grew up into rocker but many of my friends are wall flowers in a dried up, boring corporate landscape. Just cogs in the machine. Most thing we rebelled for are absolutely commonplace now. Even the dumb shit. The goths and punks were considered far left back then, but now they'd barely meet centrist while holding the exact same ideals. Time is a funny thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently running: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279855-chicago-gary-by-night-omerta-players-probably-want-to-skip-this-post\" target=\"_blank\">Gary/Chicago By Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1263-schwartzung","name":"Schwartzung","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T13:07:34-07:00","id":1521216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521213#post1521213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox doesn't necessarily need to make their money back right away on V5. They bought the brand like most companies do, to invest in the brand and hopefully grow it into an ultimately profitable venture. Record labels are built off of this methodology, fund the band, make the money back off of sale. If sales are lacking, are there signifiers of an upward trend? Online activity, good youtube analytics, well attended live shows etc? Is there a reason to continue investing in this brand? Its hard to say right now with the limited information we have. Has V5 been profitable? I'd hazard to guess yes. I have seen many requests for a second printing of CbN and CotBG, so that would indicate either folks don't know where to buy these books, or that they are indeed sold out. Since buying them without the V5 book would be rather pointless, I think it'd be safe to say that at least an equal number of those units have sold. So the question becomes &quot;what was the initial number?&quot; Who knows. And none of this accounts for illegally downloaded pdfs which the business also accounts for, and may show potential future positive returns.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chicago-by-night-for-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-ed\" target=\"_blank\">Chicago</a> an <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/cults-of-the-blood-gods-for-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-ed\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Gods</a> are easy, because we know what their kickstarters were like.<br /> <br /> Blood gods was 1550 kickstarted physical copies, let's say they did 30% more, hoping to move them via IPR, store backers or late backers. That's 2000ish copies. Not something to rave about<br /> Chicaggo was 1400 kickstarted physical copies, let's again be generous and say they printed 2000 copies.<br /> <br /> That's it. That's what was out in the world. These books were NOT generally available, and them being sold out is a facet of their limited production run, not of a huge demand for them. Them becoming available for the general populace happened for the first time with the reprints and I'm really curious how well those did.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T14:54:43-07:00","id":1521225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521187#post1521187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm confused at the idea anyone can be a vampire fan and worry about &quot;wokeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a fucking counter-culture PUNK game.<br /> <br /> Hating capitalism, loving minorities, and being accepting of everyone while being pissed off about the state of the world is baked into its DNA.<br /> <br /> Chicago by Night 1st Edition was the most diverse RPG supplement of all time for races, cultures, sexual identities, and other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh punk isn't automatically woke and vice versa theirs some overlap but they are distinct. For example I wouldn't consider middle class guy rambling about diversity in shitty Disney live actions is as far from punk as you can get likewise I would never ever consider gg allin 'woke'.<br /> <br /> God only knows what terms you'd use to describe gg politically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T21:54:29-07:00","id":1521231,"title":"","content":"Being &quot;woke&quot; just means being aware of racial injustice and prejudice. While the punk movement has always been more anti-capitalist/anti-authority I'd argue that you can't really be punk without also being woke. And you can't really be woke without being a bit punk. Racial injustice is just too heavily intertwined with economic, political and judicial injustice in the US to oppose one without really opposing all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T22:16:51-07:00","id":1521232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521213#post1521213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok Imma reply to a bunch of shit in one post 'cause I'm lazy</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want me to run you through the... not well designed steps to multi-quote on the forum, I can help you out. It's not the worst, but... it isn't nearly as good as it could be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're right, it WAS counter-culture punk game. </div> </div> </div>I think it could have stayed truer to it's cultural origins for longer. Requiem dropped &quot;punk&quot; from it's primary themes to focus on the Gothic origins of modern vampire fiction, but they left a lot of room to get your punk on in it. With every Covenant capable of being The Man, or The Rebellion, you can get into a lot of the diversity in the different eras and types of punks, instead of punks really being regulared to the Brujah and Anarchs in VtM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> however, define &quot;punk&quot; </div> </div> </div>Someone that attempts success at a profitable activity they have no formal training or preexisting practical skill in; frequently relying on a flair for showmanship to counter their reliance on their limited technical skills. Also describes the DIY and self-taught music of the 1960s and 19070s evolution of garage bands at the time by embracing their rough, simple, and aggressive music instead of attempting purposeful skill improvement over time, as well as the highly-independent and anti-authoritarian subculture that grew around these bands and their purposefully antagonistic-to-industry approach.<br /> <br /> Yes, I do know where the word originally came from. :P<br /> <br /> CT does know this too, he's just more optimistic than us about old school punk still being relevant to modern times instead of needing a new wave for a new decade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I recall, and correct me if I'm wrong, Mr Dawkins merely mentioned that a Brujah *could* be a nazi, can caught all sorts of hell for that. Therein lies the issue with &quot;wokeness&quot;, that I think people have a problem with. If a storyteller can't even paint the &quot;bad guy&quot;, how can they possibly write in the player defeating the &quot;man&quot; </div> </div> </div>There's a key bit of missing context to what Matthew drew heat for this comment. The V5 Brujah write-up has a very poorly worded section where it puts an alt-right Nazi, a public defender that refuses to give up despite how broken the US justice system is, and an Internet music pirate in the same moral category of &quot;rebels from within the system.&quot; The &quot;Brujah aren't all good people, and some are Nazis,&quot; was felt as dismissive because it demonstrated a lack of appreciation for the complaint at hand (wildly different kinds of people being lumped together in a very tone deaf fashion), and reinforced the idea that V5 (prompted by some dumbass things Martin Ericsson said) wasn't going to actually address the context of Nazi Punks and how that relates to the Brujah (esp. during an era of re-surging far-right nationalism making neo-Nazis far less fringe and far less rebellious in their causes). Which was born out in the final text where we got a fairly weak statement that supposedly passionate and motivated Brujah embrace without any real care for what their childer believed in as why there are Nazi Brujah. A very blown chance to lay the ground work for tackling some serious issues in the game.<br /> <br /> There's also the problem with the text coming off as supporting &quot;good guy Nazis&quot; as playable characters because of all this.<br /> <br /> It wasn't some giant objection to the idea of the Brujah having a Nazi problem, or having Nazi vampires at all (we definitely love the idea of watching Nazi vampires burning in the sun), but a very both-sides approach to what should be considered &quot;encouraged&quot; to play.<br /> <br /> Or the shorter version: I want to punch Nazis in the game, not have to punch someone I'm playing with because they insist that I should be cool with them playing a cool Nazi PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new games are in a way being forced into a level of wokeness by a small but vocal minority, not to mention, through the eyes of 2015-2023, some things have become simply unacceptable that were totally acceptable in 1990. </div> </div> </div>The thing is... the &quot;forced by a small vocal minority&quot; narrative doesn't really work. That small vocal minority despises corporate performative gestures as the insincere pandering it is. Companies are doing it because the social norms have moved for the majority and they need to pretend to care for the much quieter people that don't care that much, but aren't going to tolerate things like Don't Ask, Don't Tell like they did in the 90s.<br /> <br /> I also really hate the temporal moral relativism thing. &quot;Woke&quot; started in the 1930s, it's not new, it's just more popular. The whole point is that most people prefer not to see things they wouldn't have approved of, but didn't care enough to change, allowing bad actors to cause problems with impunity. That's why Black people needed to stay woke. They couldn't trust the majority of white people to stand up for them if the cops went to far, so they had to learn to be aware of what kind of town they were in and behavior accordingly for their safety. During the Civil Right era, white allies picked up on being woke for their own safety, as well as being able to help create safer communities by seeing the signs of danger thus knowing what to disrupt. The BLM protests were just the next version of the same thing, and like the last time with more support.<br /> <br /> A lot of this shit was never &quot;acceptable&quot; in &quot;polite&quot; society.&quot; It was acceptable out of sight so people that knew it was happening could be in denial about their moral culpability. That's why news cameras in the Civil Rights era, and cell phones now, are so powerful: they force people to see the stuff they used to be able to pretend wasn't the way things were, and have to confront that they don't actually want to accept it. You open people's eyes. They get woke. Because you stripped them of their blinders.<br /> <br /> I can live just fine with the fact that old school WW did a lot of racist things out of ignorance and even some well meaning but ignorant ideas. But there's a difference between it have no negative consequences in the 90s, and it being acceptable. I don't stand by it ever being acceptable; just understandable. One of the reasons WW managed to get so much good will despite all those things is because they never shied away from getting called out, and then put in work to try to make their books better. They knew they didn't have to listen, but they chose to listen, because they knew it wasn't really acceptable, just something they could get away with. And like good people, they put doing right over doing wrong that the people you hurt can't do anything about once they had it brought to their attention. It wasn't perfect, but it was consistent progress.<br /> <br /> That's what I've never seen out of Paradox. That's why they're not really &quot;woke&quot; or bowing to some &quot;woke&quot; minority. It's pandering because it's good for their wallets. Paradox has plenty of money if they want to flip off a bunch of Twitter blowhards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back in the 90s we were all about the individual. &quot;Let me be me&quot; Now it seems &quot;me&quot; must fit into a box for someone else to fight for, and feel better at night. Otherwise I completely agree. Fuck, I AM one of those dudes </div> </div> </div>Intersectionality is a real thing though. Even the conservative majority SCOTUS had to acknowledge that bias goes beyond individual actions.<br /> <br /> The &quot;let me be me&quot; attitude was fairly successful (though lots of folks got left out), but that success was also it's own enemy: It made the focus on individual actions, while institutional bias and systemic bias continued to make it way harder for some people to be themselves. &quot;I realized gay people have the right to be gay because that's none of my business,&quot; didn't magically make gay marriage legal, or force adoption agencies to be less biased towards non-traditional couples. Those sorts of fights actually got harder instead of easier, because suddenly &quot;let me be me,&quot; meant, &quot;vote for politicians that are going to let folks be themselves over whatever other things you want to see out of them&quot; and that meant pushback because it wasn't the easy, &quot;I'm not a bigot, so I'm just going to put a bit more effort into my personal life to make sure I'm being a respectful cool person to be around,&quot; and meant actually caring about other people, not just leaving them alone.... even if the result was so they could actually have the right to be themselves without assholes getting in their way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox doesn't necessarily need to make their money back right away on V5. They bought the brand like most companies do, to invest in the brand and hopefully grow it into an ultimately profitable venture. </div> </div> </div>It is worth noting though, that from the beginning, and even on their website right now, their position is tat profit is from expanding outside of the TTRPG space. The music industry doesn't entirely apply because you don't sign on an artist to make their albums into movies and video games. Maybe, just maybe, you buy a back catalog because it's a great money maker for licensing (The Beatles being the archetypal example), but record execs expect to make their money on music, not action figures of the band.<br /> <br /> One of the problems for the WoD5 games is Paradox doesn't actually need them to be profitable. They just don't want the PR mess of dumping the TTRPG. One good videogame's worth of profits is plenty for what they paid for all this to turn thing around. If Bloodlines 2 was out, and was even just an OK game that's never going to be the cult classic of 1, but enough people buy because of 1, Paradox would at least be in the black on the buyout. Easy. We wouldn't be talking about their finances around all this. It's how lackluster their video games have been that's put more of a spotlight on the TTRPGs, because it's on the TTRPGs to convince people that the brand has value now that BL 2 went into development hell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwartzung</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521214#post1521214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're aging yourself my friend hahaha!</div> </div> </div> </div>Never been shy about that around here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the 90s were the first time in a long time that we were free from fear. </div> </div> </div>I... really think that depended on who you were. The Rodney King riots and the OJ Simpson case made it very clear that being Black in the US was still dangerous. I already mentioned Don't Ask, Don't Tell; though it's a great example of how the &quot;let me be me&quot; didn't really work that well. Dry Feet/Wet Feet made the second half of the 90s a time when Cubans got really nervous. Ruby Ridge, Waco, and the Oklahoma City bombing showed a rising tension that's only gotten worse. Columbine didn't exactly end the decade on a hopeful note.<br /> <br /> I didn't feel free from fear in the 90s. But the 90s were a shift from external threats to internal threats over what to fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521225#post1521225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God only knows what terms you'd use to describe gg politically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Misanthropic anarcho-primitivism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T06:23:45-07:00","id":1521254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521216#post1521216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chicago-by-night-for-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-ed\" target=\"_blank\">Chicago</a> an <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/cults-of-the-blood-gods-for-vampire-the-masquerade-5th-ed\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Gods</a> are easy, because we know what their kickstarters were like.<br /> <br /> Blood gods was 1550 kickstarted physical copies, let's say they did 30% more, hoping to move them via IPR, store backers or late backers. That's 2000ish copies. Not something to rave about<br /> Chicaggo was 1400 kickstarted physical copies, let's again be generous and say they printed 2000 copies.<br /> <br /> That's it. That's what was out in the world. These books were NOT generally available, and them being sold out is a facet of their limited production run, not of a huge demand for them. Them becoming available for the general populace happened for the first time with the reprints and I'm really curious how well those did.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Remember when Cults was supposed to go to retail the Renegade takeover of the V5 line had started and those books were pulled from distribution. It\u2019s my understanding Renegade has rereleased it with their edits and Chicago by Night is being rereleased as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T07:19:52-07:00","id":1521255,"title":"","content":"Punk sucks and it was never good. The music sucks and the subculture sucks. And I'm not talking about pop punk at all either, I'm talking about real punk acts like The Clash, Crass, Rage Against The Machine, The Circle Jerks, The Germs, Bikini Kill, The Dead Kennedys, etc. Punk fucking sucks.<br /> <br /> I've dealt with the punk subculture before. A lot of the people who abused me in the past were often either part of the punk subculture or were supportive of it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, in my experience, punk is just conformity that's masquerading as rebellious non-conformity. There, I fucking said it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-23-2023, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T08:07:19-07:00","id":1521256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521254#post1521254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember when Cults was supposed to go to retail the Renegade takeover of the V5 line had started and those books were pulled from distribution. It\u2019s my understanding Renegade has rereleased it with their edits and Chicago by Night is being rereleased as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, and that's what caused the upsurge in interest in V5 last year. When they popped up from Renegade was the first time these books were generally available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T10:11:25-07:00","id":1521263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521255#post1521255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punk sucks and it was never good. The music sucks and the subculture sucks. And I'm not talking about pop punk at all either, I'm talking about real punk acts like The Clash, Crass, Rage Against The Machine, The Circle Jerks, The Germs, Bikini Kill, The Dead Kennedys, etc. Punk fucking sucks.<br /> <br /> I've dealt with the punk subculture before. A lot of the people who abused me in the past were often either part of the punk subculture or were supportive of it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, in my experience, punk is just conformity that's masquerading as rebellious non-conformity. There, I fucking said it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My musical tastes ran towards Rob Zombie, David Bowie, Linkin Park, P!nk, Ozzy Osbourne, and at one time, Blink-182, Limp Biskit and Avril Lavagine myself as I never could get into punk genre that much. Same with Techno that was just one word seemingly repeated over and over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T12:40:50-07:00","id":1521270,"title":"","content":"As for the 1990's while I do miss some of that time where I had less grey in my hair and had way more energy and didn't need as much sleep and could eat what I want without gaining weight or needing tums or Pepto Bismal. I certainly wouldn't view it as peaceful time. Remember during that time we had the first World Trade Center Bombing, The terrible ending in Waco Texas for the Branch Davidians, Okolama Bombing, Columbine and some shootings in my neck of the woods, The L.A. Riots after Rodney King and lets not forget O.J. Simpson trail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T13:01:20-07:00","id":1521274,"title":"","content":"I don't see a lot of value in debating musical tastes. But I think punk is worth defending on a different level, and this goes back to the future of VtM, which is innovation.<br /> <br /> Most punk music is trash because punk music started, as I defined previously, with a bunch of people that not only didn't know how to play or sing, but steadfastly insisted on figuring things out for themselves. Of course that's going to produce a lot of garbage. Punk is a genre that's perpetually stuck in an &quot;experimental&quot; phase. Whenever you think of a good band having an experimental phase, you're rarely thinking about the best music (even if it can mean some great music once they take what they learned from it into what they were doing before). There's pretty much nothing in pop music over the past 40 years that doesn't owe something to earlier punk innovations.<br /> <br /> The punk subculture is where things started going bad (though this happens to most music inspired subcultures really). Punk bands that started getting good (or at least mainstream successful) drew the ire of their early fans for losing touch with being &quot;real&quot; punks, instead of praise for putting out better music. Punk subculture is a strange brew of radical conservative mindedness (not conservative politics, conservative in a more general sense). It's under a constant tension of wanting innovative, experimental, and hard edgy music, while also railing against bands once they figure out stuff that works and that starts appealing to outsiders as well.<br /> <br /> You're not going to find many punks bragging about how punk gave us Blondie... because Blondie's early days as punk was completely unremarkable. But what they learned as young punks when they moved into new wave and disco made them huge because they were bringing in tricks,and concepts,and arrangements nobody else was. And that's one of many examples of punk bands that moved on to other genres where fans wanted what they were doing, instead of wanting them to stay how they were.<br /> <br /> Which is where we get back to punk and how it relates to Vampire. This is why the Anarchs didn't last as the default PC group and lost to people wanting to play the Camarilla. The longer you're a punk, the more you end up in one of two places: a perpetual loser because you reject everything that winning brings with it, or a sellout because you became what you thought as bad until you realized the maybe there's a reason some things are the way they are. Both the Anarchs and the (Revised era at least) Sabbat leaned into the dramatic tension caused by the idea of a society of individualists. Societies, and punks are no different as a subculture, come with norms, rules, laws, and other collective measures so they can work as a group, which they requires a lot of backbreaking mental gymnastics to try and claim is all about protecting people's right to be hardcore individualists that don't answer to The Man. &quot;Sheep go to Heaven, goats go to Hell.&quot; And there weren't many goats in either (esp. not ones that actually stuck around for long). Meanwhile the Camarilla was ultimately the most honest faction about what it wanted out of new vampires. They made no bones about being an unfair authoritarian hierarchy, were the fight to the top is hard, and vicious, and the odds of successes suck. <br /> <br /> I as noted before, Requiem stopped using the term punk to describe itself for a reason.<br /> <br /> Punk isn't useful to Vampire as an avenue of political allegory to make statements for or against causes. Punk is good for political allegory when you want to talk about movements that eat their own tails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T13:06:50-07:00","id":1521275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520736-what-do-you-think-they-are-going-to-do-for-v6?p=1521231#post1521231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being &quot;woke&quot; just means being aware of racial injustice and prejudice. While the punk movement has always been more anti-capitalist/anti-authority I'd argue that you can't really be punk without also being woke. And you can't really be woke without being a bit punk. Racial injustice is just too heavily intertwined with economic, political and judicial injustice in the US to oppose one without really opposing all of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have been true once, but it's not what most people means by woke nowaday. The term is mostly used derogatively, to describe hypocrites activists who under the cover of awareness to injustice, shows the deepest prejudiced and irrational hatred. <br /> I mean, when the european union and various european leaders are having meetings over &quot;the danger of american wokism&quot; you know it's no longuer about being aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T14:16:03-07:00","id":1521280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anubis is right and the attempt as distinction is also meaningless here. The very forces that are attempting to redefine what being woke means in terms of public conscience not only know very well what it means but are also people that are.......surprise surprise racist, bigoted shitheads who are looking to shape society and maintain systemic hatred against certain classes of people in place and to build on that foundation. &quot;Woke&quot; as pejorative in the modern conservative vernacular by and large exists so that the people using it as such can pretend to themselves and others that they are not in fact hateful scum through a softening and manipulation of language.<br /> <br /> Someone telling me they are concerned about wokeism in their media is a massive red flag to me that such a person is trying to be dishonest about their bigotry. And if such people want to start backpedaling and claim their either supposedly criticizing what they see as hypocrisy or their criticizing technical execution weaknesses in pieces of media, which is another popular smokescreen people will use it as a pejorative for. Then those people need to learn how to use better language to say what they mean rather than feeding into an increasingly fascist political force that is happily following the steps towards genocide of vulnerable groups.<br /> <br /> Got zero tolerance for that crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that people calling out woke are racist bigoted and so on is a pretty empty accusation. &quot;anti wokism&quot; sentiment is pretty much shared across the populations that have been exposed to this american idea. You find this opposition as much in the american right wing as in the french socialists.<br /> <br /> Woke is pejorative because people calling themselves wokes show themselves as amongs the most bigoted, racists, authoritarian and hateful people in modern western culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T14:38:41-07:00","id":1521284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> 